{"source":"github","project_id":"bookdown-demo","target":"rstudio/bookdown-demo","id":"pr/34","ref":34,"title":"Exit _build.sh with error when any of it's subtasks fail","description":"`set -ev` prints every command executed and fails the entire script when\r\nany command fails. This prevents false-positive cases where only one of\r\nthe tasks fails. For instance when there are LaTeX specific errors which\r\nonly cause the `bookdown::pdf_book` script to fail. In this case Travis still\r\nmarks a pull request as if the build passes.","published_at":"2018-10-01T18:36:51Z","updated_at":"2018-10-01T19:57:32Z","url":"https://github.com/rstudio/bookdown-demo/pull/34","type":"pr","extra":{"author":"qurben","merged_at":"2018-10-01T19:57:32Z","state":"MERGED"}}
